    text: '**An updater for Ultimate** (#221387): an assessment; nothing is built yet. It\'s medium, about +400 / −40 lines: one small new extension, plus moving the existing fast-forward code into a shared helper. Nothing in `server/` or `bin/` changes.\n\n**What it found:**\n- **Most of it exists already:** the fetch with its SSH/HTTPS fallback, the fast-forward with its refusals, and the "core changed · restart" item, which already appears after a pull that touches `server/`.\n- **A real gap:** moves fast-forward the *project* checkout, never the Ultimate clone. So on a machine where Ultimate runs a different project, like poe2-rust on haza-pc, the clone never updates today.\n\n**The recommended design:**\n- **Checking:** every running Ultimate checks its clone, but at most one real `git fetch` per clone per hour, plus once at startup; git\'s own `FETCH_HEAD` timestamp is shared, so several projects on one clone don\'t each fetch. Counting the new commits is local and free. It doesn\'t need the machine home, so the Mac works without `setup:machine`.\n- **Status line:** shows `↓ 5 new` only when the clone is behind. Its popover lists the commit subjects, a DiffsHub link for the range, and what they touch (extensions/web reload by themselves, server ⚠, lockfile ⚠). Buttons: **Later** and **Update now**.\n- **Update now:** fast-forward, `pnpm install` if the lockfile changed, then a short report: what reloaded by itself, where "core changed · restart" now appears, and a note if `bin/` changed.\n- **Refusals:** a dirty clone, another branch or a diverged branch get a message and an **Ask @sync** link. It never stashes, rebases or resets.\n- **ROG:** this clone is also the project, and landings keep it current, so normally nothing shows. Updates are refused while the lander is landing.\n- **Events:** `update.applied` and `update.refused` appear in the System stream and in @sync\'s feedback.\n\n**Easier alternative:** about 80 lines. Only the `↓ 5 new` badge with the commit list and a "copy command" button for `git pull --ff-only && pnpm install`. No one-click update and no refusal messages.\n\nDecisions (my picks are 1a, 2a, 3a, 4a, 5a, go):\n1. **Scope:** (a) the full flow with the Update button; (b) badge plus copy command only.\n2. **Restart after a core change:** (a) you click "core changed · restart" in each running Ultimate; (b) it restarts by itself once that instance is idle.\n3. **Interval:** (a) hourly plus at startup; (b) every 30 min.\n4. **ROG:** (a) refuse only while the lander is landing; (b) never update a clone that is also a project, badge only.\n5. **@sync\'s role:** (a) only an "Ask @sync" link when an update is refused, plus the events; (b) @sync runs every update.\n\nReply e.g. "1a 2a 3a 4a 5a, go".',
