    text: "**The updater is ready to try** (#221387): http://127.0.0.1:35341. It's a test instance. Click `↓ 5 new · update` at the bottom right. Its reviewer is still running.\n\n**What you'll see:**\n- **Behind:** \"main is 5 commits behind origin/main\", the commit subjects, a DiffsHub ↗ link, then what the range touches (extensions, web, server, lockfile) and what each needs: extensions and web reload by themselves; server means restart this Ultimate and every other one running from this clone; lockfile means `pnpm install`. Then **Update now**.\n- **Refused:** an amber `⚠ 5 new` and \"Can't update: the checkout has uncommitted changes. Nothing was stashed, rebased or reset.\", with **Ask @sync**.\n- **Updated:** `✓ updated · restart`, with the range, the install result and **Restart now**.\n- **On a phone:** the label shortens to `↓ 5 new` or `✓ restart`.\n\nTo see the other states in the preview, switch them from the browser console:\n```js\nfetch('/api/extensions/update/actions/demo',{method:'POST',headers:{'content-type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({args:{state:'refused'}})})\n```\nThe states are `behind`, `refused`, `updated` and `current`. Reload after switching.\n\n**Checked:** I looked at the \"behind\" screenshot, and it reads clearly. On a scratch clone the real update fast-forwarded 3 commits, and a dirty scratch clone was refused with its change kept. Your real clone wasn't touched. Screenshots are in `/tmp/shots-221387/` (behind, refused and updated, desktop and phone).\n\n**Differences from the plan:**\n- A clone that isn't on origin's default branch is refused.\n- A failed `pnpm install` retries on the next update.\n\nApprove it?\n1. Yes, submit once the review is clean.\n2. Change something first (tell me what).",
