    rec: [0, 0],
    text: '**Why boxer sleeps on the Mac and ultimate doesn\'t here:** it\'s the idle-release setting, `cloud.idleRelease`.\n- **Default, 10 minutes:** when a project runs nothing for 10 minutes (no conversation, no lander run, no automation due), its machine uploads a snapshot, frees the project and shows "Released · resume here". The Mac uses this default.\n- **ROG:** `~/.ultimate/settings.json` here has `"idleRelease": 0` (never). We set that on 2026-10-18 so ROG would keep the project.\n\nSince boxer is released, it also disappears from the fleet page, which only lists projects with a running machine.\n\n**Fix it on the Mac now:** add `"idleRelease": 0` under `cloud` in its `~/.ultimate/settings.json`, restart Ultimate there, and click **Resume here** once.\n\n**For good** (my picks are 1a, 2a): idle release made sense when the cloud held a copy you could open anywhere. Now you connect over Tailscale to whichever machine runs a project, so releasing it only makes it unreachable until you click Resume, and **Back up now** covers the backup side.\n\n1. **Idle release:** (a) delete it: a machine keeps a project until you move it or stop Ultimate cleanly; (b) keep it, but default to 0 (never); (c) leave it as is.\n2. **Fleet page:** (a) also list released projects quietly, e.g. "boxer · free · last on sentry-mac", linking to that machine\'s page with **Resume here**; (b) keep listing only running projects.\n\nReply e.g. "1a 2a".',
