    text: '**Setup health is ready to try** (#222679): http://127.0.0.1:43145. It\'s a test instance with three made-up warnings. Its reviewer is still running.\n\n**What you\'ll see:**\n- **Status line:** "⚠ 3 setup issues" (on a phone, "⚠ 3"). It\'s hidden entirely when nothing needs attention. It replaces the separate "N secrets missing" and "provider failing" items.\n- **Popover**, headed "What isn\'t set up on this machine, and what it costs". Each warning says what it costs and has a fix button:\n  - **Summary model:** "openai-codex/gpt-6-luna: no login here. Using openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5 instead for titles, codemode step lines, message triage and question cards." [Choose]\n  - **Agent models:** "lander, reviewer, reviewer-correctness, reviewer-simplicity, reviewer-architecture → openai-codex: no login here. They fail at their first model call, so landings fail." [Log in]\n  - **Secrets:** "PARALLEL_API_KEY missing." [Add]\n  - Quieter rows below: cloud sync, Tailscale, providers ok, lander checks.\n- **Summary model fallback:** when the default has no login, it switches to the first available of a known-good list (Luna, Haiku 5.5, openrouter Haiku 5.5, …) and tells you once. A model you set yourself only gets a warning.\n- **My side:** a hidden note on my next input whenever the set of warnings changes, and one more when they clear.\n\nI looked at the desktop popover: clear and quiet, with each fix one click away. This is exactly what would have shown on the Mac today. Screenshots: `/tmp/shots-222679/desktop-popover.png`, `phone.png`, `phone-popover.png`, `none.png`.\n\nApprove it?\n1. Yes, submit once the review is clean.\n2. Change something first (tell me what).',
