    rec: [null],
    text: '**Proposal: stop provider alerts for single passing failures.** @sync has now woken several times today for one-off failures on ROG:\n- Claude Code: "request failed" twice, each right after a successful call;\n- Claude Code: Anthropic "overloaded" twice, with successes 0.3 s and 6.6 s before;\n- openai-codex: one timeout this morning that recovered.\n\nEach one set the provider to "failing", woke @sync for a turn, and @sync concluded each time that nothing was wrong.\n\n**Fix, small:** a provider counts as failing only after 2–3 failures in a row, or a failure with no success in the last few minutes. Capacity errors (`overloaded`, rate limits) never count as failing, since they\'re Anthropic\'s problem rather than your login. A real login or auth error still alerts right away. That changes provider health, which the new setup-health item and @sync both read, so both get quieter.\n\nShould I start it?\n1. Yes, as a small change.\n2. Leave it.',
