    opts: [2, 2, 2, 2],
    rec: [0, 0, 0, 0],
    text: '**A more detailed extension overview** (#230861): an assessment; nothing is built yet. It\'s small to medium, about +200 lines, with no restart if decision 3a works out.\n\n**Inline expand rather than a modal.** Each row gets a chevron; clicking it opens the details right there, and the on/off toggle stays in the row. On a phone a modal would cover the list you\'re browsing, and with ~45 rows opening one at a time keeps your place. Details load only when you open a row.\n\nFor your `laravel` extension, the expanded row would show:\n```\n▾ laravel  this project · its folder                    [●]\n  Laravel Boost MCP (php artisan boost:mcp) as one agent tool.\n  TOOLS 1\n   laravel   Call a Laravel Boost MCP tool (routes, schema…)\n  PROVIDES — · NEEDS — · WANTS —\n  ACTIONS — · DOCUMENTS — · EVENTS —\n  PROMPT 1 section · 0 hooks\n  ~/Projects/boxer/.ultimate/extensions/laravel\n```\nEmpty groups fold into one dim line, and a busier one like `board` lists its tool, actions, events and what it provides and needs.\n\n**What it needs:**\n- **Already in the browser:** tool names, actions, prompt sections, secrets, load errors, the README and the web parts (panels, slots, commands).\n- **Missing:** tool descriptions, and what each extension provides, needs and wants. A small read-only action adds them.\n\n**Easier alternative:** names only, with no new action, about 80 lines. It drops tool descriptions, which is the "what does this tool do" part you asked about, so I don\'t recommend it.\n\n**Limits:**\n- The panel shows the extensions of the instance it runs in, so boxer\'s appear only on boxer\'s own page.\n- A switched-off extension shows "off: tools load when it\'s on".\n\n**Decisions** (my picks: 1a 2a 3a 4a, go):\n1. **Layout:** (a) inline expand; (b) a modal from an ⓘ button.\n2. **Data:** (a) the new read-only action, with tool descriptions and provides/needs/wants; (b) names only.\n3. **Tool descriptions:** (a) read them without touching core, if possible; (b) a one-line core change that needs a restart.\n4. **Full contract text** (`api.ts`/`refs.ts`) in the row: (a) no, the summary and counts are enough; (b) a "show contract" fold.\n\nIt\'s UI, so you\'ll get a preview before it lands. Reply e.g. "1a 2a 3a 4a, go".',
