    n: 3,
    opts: [2, 2, 2],
    rec: [0, 0, 0],
    text: "**The transcript losing the bottom after you send** (#230946): an assessment; nothing is built yet.\n\n**Yesterday's fix works:** sending from a scrolled-up position, from the bottom, at phone width, and with late codemode summary lines all stayed pinned on a test instance.\n\n**The cause of what you still see** is the browser's own scroll anchoring. When a row above the view shrinks while the last row grows in the same moment, Chrome moves the scroll position up to keep the shrinking row on screen. The scroll library we use (`use-stick-to-bottom`) can't tell that from you scrolling up, so it stops following until you scroll down or send again. Real runs do exactly this often:\n- a codemode summary line replaces a longer raw header;\n- \"working · N steps\" folds into its list as the next row arrives;\n- the \"working…\" line disappears as the answer appears;\n- a triage verdict or a divider swaps in.\n\nOn the test instance, forcing that change un-stuck the view by 150 px, and later growth wasn't followed. With anchoring off, it stayed at the bottom.\n\nThere's a smaller second trigger: loading older history mid-run can switch following off while the smooth scroll is still catching up.\n\n**Caveat:** this was reproduced by forcing the layout shift on a test instance. Your real conversation was idle, so no live failure was captured.\n\n**Fix:** small, about 10 lines in `web/src/app/transcript.tsx`.\n- Turn anchoring off only while the view follows the bottom. When you've scrolled up to read, anchoring stays on, so a summary changing above you doesn't move your text.\n- Stop following on a history load only when you've actually left the bottom.\n- Same library, nothing new installed.\n\n**Regression test:** a new browser test (about 120 lines) at desktop and phone width. It forces exactly that layout shift and asserts the view stays at the bottom. It also sends from a scrolled-up position, and checks that scrolling up mid-run still stops following. It fails on today's code. There was no test like this before, which is why the bug could keep coming back.\n\n**Easier alternative:** anchoring off always (one CSS line). It fixes the bug, but when you're scrolled up reading, a row above you that changes height shifts your text.\n\nDecisions (my picks: 1a 2a 3a):\n1. **Fix:** (a) anchoring off only while following, plus the history-load fix; (b) anchoring off always.\n2. **Test:** (a) add the browser regression test; (b) fix only, checked on a preview.\n3. **Go:** (a) build it now, with a preview for you before it lands; (b) first catch a real failure in this conversation during a live run.\n\nReply e.g. \"1a 2a 3a\". The extension overview (message 1291) is also still waiting on you.",
