    text: "**The scroll fix is ready to try** (#230946): http://127.0.0.1:42755/?conversation=39. It's a test instance with 800 seeded entries; send `phases demo` or `codemode steps demo`. Its reviewer is still running.\n\n**What changed** (`web/src/app/transcript.tsx`):\n- While the view follows the bottom, the browser's scroll anchoring is off, so it can no longer push the view up.\n- Loading older history stops following only when you've actually left the bottom.\n- When you've scrolled up to read, anchoring stays on, so your text doesn't move.\n\n**The forced layout shift** (a row above shrinks while the last row grows, then 200 px more), distance from the bottom:\n- before: 0 → 150 → 150 → 350, with the ↓ button and following lost;\n- after: 0 → 0 → 0 → 1, with no ↓ button.\n\n**Rechecked:**\n- **Send while scrolled up:** sent from 1,391 px up, it stayed pinned at the bottom.\n- **Scroll up mid-run:** following stops and the ↓ button appears.\n- **Paging upward through history:** your place didn't move across 4 pages.\n- **Phone width:** it ends at the bottom.\n- **Not tested:** a real phone with momentum scrolling.\n\nI looked at the screenshot after the forced shift: the view sits at the bottom with no ↓ button. Screenshots are in `/tmp/scroll-230946/`: `after-anchor-shift.png`, `after-midrun-scrollup.png`, `after-phone.png`, and the before state `desk-anchor-shift.png`.\n\nSubmit it once the review is clean?\n1. Yes.\n2. Change something first (tell me what).",
