    text: "**Branch prompts in boxer's project context:** I read boxer's root (#1) from here.\n\n**What's in there:** each branch start copies its full prompt into the context, as \"#3873 was started from the tally … with the prompt: You are a coordinator. **Size: small, clear access fix…**\". Six of those take about 16k characters, nearly as much as all 19 abstracts. Branches start from this context, so every new branch also reads all those old prompts.\n\n**My take:** you're right, they don't belong there in full.\n- **Instructions meant for one branch:** most of a prompt is \"size, run the reviewer, then submit\". That's noise for later branches.\n- **Already covered:** each branch's abstract already opens with an \"Ask:\" line that says what it was asked, and it stays current.\n- **What's useful:** that a branch exists and what it's for, so siblings don't duplicate work. One line does that.\n\n**Proposal** (small, one coordinator, no UI change): a branch start records only a one-line intent with its breadcrumb, e.g. \"#3873 started by @ultimate: restrict department writes to admins\". The full prompt stays in the branch's own conversation. This applies to every project, this one included; existing entries shrink when the context is next compacted.\n\n**\"You are a coordinator.\":** I don't start prompts that way, and it isn't needed, since a branch already runs with the coordinator instructions. It points at something bigger: the lander noted that boxer's @ultimate gets its `laravel` tool \"through a project copy of agents/ultimate.md in .ultimate\". That copy overrides the built-in, so boxer's @ultimate never gets updates to my instructions. That fits what I saw earlier: its system prompt still lacked the new coordinator boundary. The fix is to let a project add a tool to @ultimate without copying its whole definition. I'd have a coordinator assess the simplest way.\n\nDecisions (my picks: 1a 2a):\n1. **Branch starts in the context:** (a) one-line intent plus breadcrumb; (b) drop them, rely on abstracts; (c) leave as is.\n2. **Boxer's copied `agents/ultimate.md`:** (a) assess a way for projects to add tools to @ultimate without forking it; (b) leave it.",
